{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview","id":860265,"title":"Milestone Preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-06T06:18:22-07:00","id":860265,"title":"Milestone Preview","content":"Sweet, finally got something: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/prometheanmilestones/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/prometheanmilestones/</a><br /> <br /> Finally got days off work and saw this in the Open Development Blog section while waiting for Pack Spoilers.<br /> <br /> I like how it seems the world/narrative bends towards finding milestones along the way. Azothic Memory is really peaking my interest, and seems exactly like the sort of thing Promethean needs since they're always stuck at Tier 1 with maybe Tier 2 if you're okay with a region going bad real quickly. <br /> <br /> So, what does everyone else think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T21:11:35-07:00","id":860769,"title":"","content":"I don't bother using tiers but I like the direction the previews are heading. Seems like 2e will be way more playable than 1e was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T22:33:38-07:00","id":860799,"title":"","content":"Hm. I don't know if you have time for it, but a suggestion: create a graphical diagram for milestones beyond the space available on a char sheet. I'm not exactly sure how you'd do this, since there are so many possibilities... but don't make it a checklist.<br /> <br /> Or... I don't know. Reading this preview made me think of art analysis. Like... in certain types of art, there's more than meets the eye to a casual, outsider viewer, but if you're familiar with the symbolic language, there are dozens of little things that are simply part and parcel to the message of the piece. So a painting about a Promethean <i>has</i> to have six essential elements that represent the universal milestones, but there's additional detail that expresses the Roles they've been in and atmospheric things that describe their personality as rendered into instinctive milestones.<br /> <br /> It just... feels right. Or... it feels wrong to just make a list of milestones achieved on a few then-blank lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T23:37:47-07:00","id":860824,"title":"","content":"The Leverage RPG has a character development model that involves writing down te Jobs you've done, and then providing a bonus whenever you work a reference to one of your completed Jobs into the current Job. I wonder if something like this could be done with Milestones: in situations where a Milestone that you've completed is appropriate, you can invoke it for some small benefit that reflects the lesson you learned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T00:35:36-07:00","id":860847,"title":"","content":"I'm glad to see a few more universal milestones thrown in, and am eager to see the prescribed milestones by Role. Other than that, the system doesn't seem as radically changed as the 2e system around it. I suppose that's fine, i wasn't clamoring for a radical revision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T05:20:00-07:00","id":860975,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m a bit disappointed \u2013 I was hoping for Milestones to work at least partially based on Aspirations-like mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That PLAYER choose some of them. I feel more hacks are coming to the Promethean 2ED than I thought will be needed...<br /> <br /> However, rest of mechanics spoiled are interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T19:00:31-07:00","id":861515,"title":"","content":"Well, that's sort of how instinctive Milestones seem to work, at least partially. They're created by the GM using the player's input as a guide and inspiration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T21:42:14-07:00","id":861583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861515#post861515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's sort of how instinctive Milestones seem to work, at least partially. They're created by the GM using the player's input as a guide and inspiration</div> </div> </div> </div>So players says &quot;Interesting would he my Created need to hate someone / love someone / kill someone&quot;. Storyteller says &quot;Lol, nope silly, you do not understand your own character&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I really get that some ( most of them even ) will be ST specific - but player should also have input in the Pilgrimage of his character, not only fullfiling STs objectives on the road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:02:09-07:00","id":861621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861583#post861583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So players says &quot;Interesting would he my Created need to hate someone / love someone / kill someone&quot;. Storyteller says &quot;Lol, nope silly, you do not understand your own character&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I really get that some ( most of them even ) will be ST specific - but player should also have input in the Pilgrimage of his character, not only fullfiling STs objectives on the road.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Instinctive Milestones are created by the ST using input from the character's player.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Aha, so what you're saying is that instinctive Milestones are created by the ST completely disregarding input from the character's player!&quot;<br /> <br /> No, wyrd. Just no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:20:28-07:00","id":861633,"title":"","content":"I pointing here to the dissonance on characters opinions - Storyteller is <i>not</i> PCs player. He is enviorment. In <b>Promethean</b> your character maybe is under massive force that want's to govern its life - but it should not shape it all.<br /> <br /> Also, I think it's really weird that characters, in-universe, cannot say &quot;I want to feel love - What will it makes me feel? Maybe it will unlock my next stage in Pilgrimage...&quot;<br /> <br /> From spoilers writing it seems that <i>all</i> Milestones are made by ST. Even if he have players best interest in mind and ask them directly - sometimes will come dissonance between what player wants to do with character and Storyteller wants to. Part of players chosen Milestones seems to solve this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:20:32-07:00","id":861634,"title":"","content":"What Satchel said. ChroD does not assume that the Storyteller and players are at odds with each other; it assumes that Storytelling is a collaborative process, and that the Storyteller will take the players' wishes into account when (in this case) choosing Milestones (instinctive in particular; but really, all of them). If you're in a group where the Storyteller and players aren't communicating properly, or where the Storyteller is choosing to disregard the players' wishes, you've got bigger problems than who defines Milestones.<br /> <br /> Also, we don't know what <b>Promethean</b>'s Five Questions are; given that Instinctive Milestones are based on them, and given that we haven't yet seen the Storyteller advice for choosing Milestones, it's a bit early to condemn the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-08-2016, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:44:35-07:00","id":861644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861583#post861583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So players says &quot;Interesting would he my Created need to hate someone / love someone / kill someone&quot;. Storyteller says &quot;Lol, nope silly, you do not understand your own character&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I really get that some ( most of them even ) will be ST specific - but player should also have input in the Pilgrimage of his character, not only fullfiling STs objectives on the road.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, I ask this with as much delicacy as I can.<br /> <br /> Do you not understand how how dialogue between text, storytellers, and players work? Do you not know how structures work in storytelling, how they are used?<br /> <br /> Actually, no. I'm not going to ask those questions. I'm just going to explain it:<br /> <br /> There are themes and motifs at work in Promethean, and they are many and complex. The spine here is the theme of deeply understanding humanity in a dialogue made up of alchemical speech and iconography. That's both a heavy topic(humanity) and a complicated 'text'(alchemy) for any one person to comprehend, let alone handle on an individual basis. That said, the game, by it's inherent nature, <i>is individual</i>. Player-Storyteller dialogue on character direction and development is essential. it is somewhat unreasonable to expect storytellers to balance the three without tools.<br /> <br /> The Instinctive Milestones are a tool-in this case, it's a funnel, a wide set of white lines to stay in between, a set of bumpers on the bowling alley of the story, a buffer to help you ensure that you hit the pins while still giving you room to live, learn, develop, and apply your own style. It gives you a direction, points that help evoke the aesthetic of alchemy and the deep questions and possible answers for humanity-in short, it gives you a guideline that makes it so that whatever you come up with will, when presented to others, make them go &quot;Ah, yes, I can clearly see that this is a Promethean game.&quot; It keeps you out of the gutters. It helps ensure that this game feels, sounds, touches like a Promethean game. It's there to ensure the Frankenstein of a duck you are making will, invariably, be not mistaken for anything other than a duck.(Except, maybe, a Frankenstein monster, because, you know, it is.)<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT! On the other hand! You'll notice each Milestone has multiple interpretations, and in fact is broad to a point of nigh-vagueness. <b><i>THIS IS DELIBERATE.</i></b> Each of these points is so loose that you cannot just say &quot;Me and the book are gonna plan out your whole honeymoon with philosophy and pizza.&quot; You will <i>flounder</i> if you try to do that. The book provides a spine, and you provide the muscles, but the player has to provide the blood and heart.<br /> <br /> What the Instinctive Milestones do is create a space for discussion between player and storyteller, a communal road for them to walk down. Instead of just going &quot;Well, okay, what do you think is the important things you need to explore about humanity to ascend to a deeper realm of being?&quot;(which is such a fucking huge and heavy and impossible question), it breaks it down into smaller, more manageable questions, like &quot;What is the fascinating thing about humanity to you? or &quot;What is the most confusing thing about humanity to you?&quot; or &quot;What about your character is broken?&quot; or any other stuff like that, and examples give you guidelines to break that down into even more manageable questions, because it asks you to ask your players about Roles and Refinements and Torment and all this stuff and what it all means to them and what it feeds out into. You then take the answers to these directed questions and turn them into story hooks, plot twists, platforms for the Great Swampy Middle and Firestorms for the Big Dramatic Climaxes. And because you have a compass(not rails), anyone can look at anyone using Instinctive Milestones and go &quot;Oh my god, what an original and powerful Promethean story.&quot; instead of &quot;Well, that was interesting, but it might have worked better as Geist/Demon/Bangarang story&quot;<br /> <br /> Instinctive Milestones are rulers and thread, slabs and gauges. They are a stage for you, the storyteller, to strap in the flesh and elements, to make a monster, and for your players strike with lightning, to make life. It is <i>not</i> an invitation have an elitist storyteller-text jerk-off session. People who think they are that are poor storytellers, and probably should not be running games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-08-2016, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:53:01-07:00","id":861646,"title":"","content":"You know what? I think it was a mistake to vote for Transmutations in the next spoiler; I think it's more important to see Promethean's Integrity substitute, Pilgrimage. Because I get the feeling that it's going to be crucially important to understanding the heart of Promethean 2e. That's where the Five Questions are going to be, for instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T23:57:38-07:00","id":861649,"title":"","content":"Was there actually vote in there? Didn't notice.<br /> <br /> But yeah, like Kuruth for Werewolf, Pilgrmage is so essential that should always be the first thing people cry for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:17:31-07:00","id":861679,"title":"","content":"So long as Milestones aren't as rare and irregular as Promethean previews, I'll be satisfied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:34:59-07:00","id":861787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861583#post861583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storyteller says &quot;Lol, nope silly, you do not understand your own character&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If my GM completely disregards the narrative hints I'm giving them in order to not only alter the perception I have of my own character's personality but to actually <i>sabotage </i>it, which is the connotation I'm getting from your theoretical example, then I'm <i>not going to play with that GM</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy</b> is a game where learning 'secret' parts of your character's personality and history is part of the fun; <b>Promethean</b> is a game where <i>you're not even a human being</i>, and you don't think it's reasonable that, in the process of <i>becoming a human being</i>, they wouldn't learn something unexpected?<br /> <br /> It's one thing to say, &quot;I want my Promethean to learn about love&quot; and the GM to tell you, &quot;Your character is destined to be a serial killer and will never know love.&quot; It's a different thing for your GM to say, &quot;Your character is blessed to learn about love by getting their heart broken&quot; or &quot;Your character will learn about love from sponsoring a recovering addict.&quot; It's a surprise but it's not a fucking derail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861633#post861633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think it's really weird that characters, in-universe, cannot say &quot;I want to feel love - What will it makes me feel? Maybe it will unlock my next stage in Pilgrimage...&quot;<br /> <br /> From spoilers writing it seems that <i>all</i> Milestones are made by ST. Even if he have players best interest in mind and ask them directly - sometimes will come dissonance between what player wants to do with character and Storyteller wants to. Part of players chosen Milestones seems to solve this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, if <i>I'm</i> the GM and I ignore the hint my PCs are telling me for the type of story they want to experience in the game then <i>I'm</i> a shit GM.<br /> <br /> But the whole point for a Promethean in-universe is that they <i>don't know</i>. Isn't that just like real life? You grow up thinking you have to learn these life lessons but then it turns out life isn't what you thought it'd be <i>at fucking all</i>, and yet those lessons you do end up learning are still valuable. That right there is a great Promethean story (that requires collaboration between PC and GM, which the game endorses): thinking you needed to experience one thing but discovering that the real lesson you needed was something else. It makes you think about your character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:35:11-07:00","id":861788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861644#post861644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instinctive Milestones are rulers and thread, slabs and gauges. They are a stage for you, the storyteller, to strap in the flesh and elements, to make a monster, and for your players strike with lightning, to make life. It is <i>not</i> an invitation have an elitist storyteller-text jerk-off session. People who think they are that are poor storytellers, and probably should not be running games.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair there's a continuum here. Some players are going to want the ST to take care of the details for them and others are going to want almost all of the milestones to work more like aspirations. There are no poor storytellers or players, there are only the stories troupes want to tell and how they want to go about it. One of the worst aspects of the old World of Darkness was how downright preachy the text often seemed regarding &quot;how&quot; the game should be played. There is honestly no such thing as &quot;doing it wrong&quot; and, one of the great things about the sandbox nature of CofD is that affords folks relief from that kind of perpetual &quot;you're doing it wrong&quot; mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:44:52-07:00","id":861863,"title":"","content":"Umm\u2026 there <i>are</i> poor Storytellers and players; I've gamed with some. And there <i>is</i> such a thing as \u201cdoing it wrong\u201d, which is behind wyrdhamster's concerns: he's worried that the Storyteller will \u201cdo it wrong\u201d, which is why he wants to take Milestones out of the Storyteller's hands. <br /> <br /> That said, I'll agree with your point that \u201cnot doing it by the book\u201d is not the same as \u201cdoing it wrong\u201d. Conversely, \u201cthe book doesn't support my preferred gaming style\u201d is not the same as \u201cthe book is doing it wrong\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:59:12-07:00","id":861872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861787#post861787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my GM completely disregards the narrative hints I'm giving them in order to not only alter the perception I have of my own character's personality but to actually <i>sabotage </i>it, which is the connotation I'm getting from your theoretical example, then I'm <i>not going to play with that GM</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you need if he is one and only <b>Promethean</b> ST in your region. Shit, maybe I'm the only one interested in running one character in my whole country! ( In reality. probably one of five as I look from one of largest RPG FB groups in Poland. ) So it can totally be &quot;we play what we can get&quot; - until some really breaks gameplay, some small misgivings pile up, there is big fight and part of team can just shut a door in middle of play. And then we have drama, spiliting groups, etc.<br /> <br /> Got it twice in recent years ( mostly from inner players incompatibility ) and I really look then over any situations where players and ST' s aims can miss so dramatically. From what I read Milestones can lead to this kind situations, even unintentionally on ST side. Maybe Five Questions will solve it in the end, but as possible <b>Promethean</b> <i>player</i> - I miss Aspirations-like Milestones. They would be safe and cool vent for players to enrich his Pilgrimage <i>on top on those shown in spoiler</i>.<br /> <br /> There is also whole <i>involuntary</i> sabotage - Storyteller has vision of character that is A, player has that is B and gameplay makes character into C that is somehow A+B. Putting whole Pilgrimage on ST is a bit step backwards - Aspirations were introduced in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> to move <i>players</i> agenda in chronicle. When ST is making all Milestones - that are heart of the <b>Promethean</b> game - it seems like <b>Promethean</b> players like to be played against dark Demiurge that is rolling with their lives all the time - and get more of this. I do not assume it's point of new Milestones, rather just can be seen that way from players perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861787#post861787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mummy</b> is a game where learning 'secret' parts of your character's personality and history is part of the fun; <b>Promethean</b> is a game where <i>you're not even a human being</i>, and you don't think it's reasonable that, in the process of <i>becoming a human being</i>, they wouldn't learn something unexpected?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>No, I did not say that.</b> I pointed that some things we learn cause we <i>want</i> to and are <i>also</i> a part of our life.<br /> <br /> My life example can point to this thing exactly - I'm bisexual, but I'm raised in largely homophobic country. For years I feared my feelings to other man, being afraid of social backslash. I was having a girlfriend for three years, but we ended relationship. Then I <i>choose</i> to look for male lover. I made gay dating profile and after few weeks found my life partner and relative happiness. I'm man that I'm now <i>cause</i> <i>I made decision</i> to pursue my dreams - not that some ST made my Milestone list. Yes, part of it was ending my relationship with my ex-girlfriend, that seemed more like some ST musings of &quot;Must live through heartbreak&quot;. But to go in to being man I'm today, I made decision. If that is not my life Milestone, I do not know what is it.<br /> <br /> Same can be talk about my job career - I went to local university of technology to study Computer Science when I was having other possibilities. Not some vengeful god putted me here, not someone marked my place here - I went to study CS and ended my studies. I wanted to become programmer, ended as IT guy, in the end, but always dreamed to work with computers. In someways I can totally see this as metaphor of living as Created. I pursued my own Milestone, ended in other resolution of it - but life lesson from this nonetheless.<br /> <br /> <b>Life is mixed bag of both <i>outer events</i> and <i>inner decisions</i> - when new Milestones reflects greatly first, I do not see the second much.</b> I <i>really</i> understand why ST need to make most of them - but few player made Milestones would only <i>enrich</i> the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861863#post861863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm\u2026 there <i>are</i> poor Storytellers and players; I've gamed with some. And there <i>is</i> such a thing as \u201cdoing it wrong\u201d, which is behind wyrdhamster's concerns: he's worried that the Storyteller will \u201cdo it wrong\u201d, which is why he wants to take Milestones out of the Storyteller's hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but only partially from ST hands. I still thinks that ST should makes <i>most</i> of Milestones - this way the chronicle story is most coherent and unexpected to players - but <b>few</b> Milestones players should choose to enrich the game experience for them and safeguard on ( unintentional ) bad ST decisions. Then it really is both parties game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-09-2016, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:39:36-07:00","id":861955,"title":"","content":"First of all, I get the feeling Jacob's been talking in response to something I said, because there's odd gaps and responses to things that aren't said. This is what we call a context clue, kids.<br /> <br /> Secondly, there is such a thing as bad storytelling, both on the part of storytellers and players. The thing to remember is that bad storytelling need not ruin a person's or group's appreciation of the event-people have fun with bad movies, bad books, bad music all the time. The <i>important</i> thing to remember is that bad storytelling does not, by itself, facilitate the enjoyment, it's an impediment that people who have fun work around in spite of it. At a bare minimum, if it makes having fun hard to do for any number of reasons, it's bad storytelling.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, the problem here is a misapprehension of the tool. You don't use a screwdriver to hammer nails, you don't put broccoli on pizza, and you don't use Instinctive Milestones to deny your players input, because that's not the function of them. Storytelling is a craft, and if someone insists on using a tool for storytelling the wrong way, that's bad storytelling.<br /> <br /> Finally, it's important to understand what is and isn't bad storytelling because it's integral to the experience. It's <i>enabling</i>, it's <i>empowering</i>. Understanding of the craft allows storytellers and players agency in the discussion for their own enjoyment out of the game, it gives them the dialogue and awareness to actually be able to contend with problematic perspectives and assertions. When you say &quot;There is no bad storytelling&quot;, you're telling people who are in groups that aren't providing for them to shut up and accept it. By creating the distinction and educating people in regards to it, you give people the ability to change and improve themselves, their environments, their lives.<br /> <br /> &quot;There is no bad storytelling&quot; is an entropic concept. &quot;There is bad storytelling&quot; is a creative one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:43:21-07:00","id":861957,"title":"","content":"Like, as a parallel, imagine if we went around saying &quot;There are no bad houses&quot;, if we tried to make that a thing. We'd be justifying shanties and lean-tos as things. But if we say &quot;There are bad houses&quot;, people make, you know, actually decent houses. Storytelling works the exact same way.<br /> <br /> &quot;There is no bad X&quot; is often the excuse of bad craftsmen who don't really want to work to make something substantial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:22:26-07:00","id":862139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861955#post861955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, I get the feeling Jacob's been talking in response to something I said, because there's odd gaps and responses to things that aren't said. This is what we call a context clue, kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the quote part of the quote communicated that. But yes, I did abbreviate what I was responding to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861955#post861955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, there is such a thing as bad storytelling, both on the part of storytellers and players. The thing to remember is that bad storytelling need not ruin a person's or group's appreciation of the event-people have fun with bad movies, bad books, bad music all the time. The <i>important</i> thing to remember is that bad storytelling does not, by itself, facilitate the enjoyment, it's an impediment that people who have fun work around in spite of it. At a bare minimum, if it makes having fun hard to do for any number of reasons, it's bad storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similarly <i>good storytelling</i> doesn't guarantee positive results. Communication between storytellers and players is key. That's why I typically talk about troupes. If the troupe agrees to leave the responsibility for something up to the ST, that's their option. Bad storytelling isn't about the choices that get made. It's <b><i>how</i></b> those choices get made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861955#post861955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thirdly, the problem here is a misapprehension of the tool. You don't use a screwdriver to hammer nails, you don't put broccoli on pizza, and you don't use Instinctive Milestones to deny your players input, because that's not the function of them. Storytelling is a craft, and if someone insists on using a tool for storytelling the wrong way, that's bad storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very orthadoxical, dogmatic approach. You can certainly use a screwdriver as a hammer if you have to. We call that improvisation. You can certainly put broccoli on pizza. It's delicious. (I certainly agree about Instinctive milestones but that isn't what we're talking about. We've wandered off-topic.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861955#post861955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, it's important to understand what is and isn't bad storytelling because it's integral to the experience. It's <i>enabling</i>, it's <i>empowering</i>. Understanding of the craft allows storytellers and players agency in the discussion for their own enjoyment out of the game, it gives them the dialogue and awareness to actually be able to contend with problematic perspectives and assertions. When you say &quot;There is no bad storytelling&quot;, you're telling people who are in groups that aren't providing for them to shut up and accept it. By creating the distinction and educating people in regards to it, you give people the ability to change and improve themselves, their environments, their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm saying at all. When I say &quot;there's no such thing as bad storytelling&quot; I'm affirming that troupes (not players and ST's individually) have every right to modify rules in order <i><b>to tell the stories that they want to tell</b></i>. It isn't just a matter of &quot;understanding craft&quot;. A good storyteller understands their players and communicates with them. Good players understand their storyteller and communicate with them. Playing RPG's is a cooperative event. I usually use the analogy of &quot;imagine you're sitting down for a play reading where everyone makes up their own parts and we roll dice to add in a pinch of randomness to resolve conflicts within the story&quot; when I have to explain role-playing games to people who haven't played them before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861955#post861955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;There is no bad storytelling&quot; is an entropic concept. &quot;There is bad storytelling&quot; is a creative one.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO &quot;there is bad storytelling&quot; is the entropic concept. It's basically saying that if one isn't being dogmatically faithful to the orthadoxy of the game's text then one isn't playing the game. Saying &quot;there is no bad storytelling&quot; is my way of affirming to troupes that they should change the game to suit their particular needs. It's okay to experiment, to hack, and to try different things. The game is a sandbox. Play it as near to or far from as the authors' intentions as you like. There is no creativity without making mistakes and trying different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 04-08-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:25:35-07:00","id":862144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861957#post861957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, as a parallel, imagine if we went around saying &quot;There are no bad houses&quot;, if we tried to make that a thing. We'd be justifying shanties and lean-tos as things. But if we say &quot;There are bad houses&quot;, people make, you know, actually decent houses. Storytelling works the exact same way.<br /> <br /> &quot;There is no bad X&quot; is often the excuse of bad craftsmen who don't really want to work to make something substantial.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are no bad houses, only poor construction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:28:39-07:00","id":862148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861863#post861863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm\u2026 there <i>are</i> poor Storytellers and players; I've gamed with some. And there <i>is</i> such a thing as \u201cdoing it wrong\u201d, which is behind wyrdhamster's concerns: he's worried that the Storyteller will \u201cdo it wrong\u201d, which is why he wants to take Milestones out of the Storyteller's hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. However, situations are quite complex. This is why knowing all the facts first is important. All to often I see people on these (and other) forums going off on a diatribe based on their assumptions. On a more philosophical note I might say that there are no poor storytellers and players, only poor situations. At the end of the day it's all about communication. In Wyrd's case, it's hard to say that the ST is the one totally in the wrong (insufficient facts). Communication is a two-way street.<br /> <br /> My real concern is affirming Wyrd's right to make hacks. Be they good hacks or bad hacks, hacking is part and parcel a part of life (and games).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861863#post861863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'll agree with your point that \u201cnot doing it by the book\u201d is not the same as \u201cdoing it wrong\u201d. Conversely, \u201cthe book doesn't support my preferred gaming style\u201d is not the same as \u201cthe book is doing it wrong\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we violently agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 04-08-2016, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T20:10:41-07:00","id":862382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862148#post862148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My real concern is affirming Wyrd's right to make hacks. Be they good hacks or bad hacks, hacking is part and parcel a part of life (and games).</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is saying that you can't hack Milestones to be entirely or partially player-determined.<br /> <br /> The issue is that Wyrd's arguments are always about the official rules. It's extremely frustrating for me, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T21:19:33-07:00","id":862405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862382#post862382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is saying that you can't hack Milestones to be entirely or partially player-determined.<br /> <br /> The issue is that Wyrd's arguments are always about the official rules. It's extremely frustrating for me, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no, if Wyrd's response was just &quot;I don't like it, I'm not using and just gonna figure out milestones with my players,&quot; I wouldn't care. In fact, I actually assume that's gonna be the default attitude. I don't care about that.<br /> <br /> My problem is a misapprehension of the tools and their application, on two fronts.<br /> <br /> First, a failure to understand that you use a hammer for nails leading to an outright rejection of hammers is clearly and obviously making things harder on anyone involved, or at the least denying themselves something that will ease the process. The construction metaphor breaks a little apart, because I'm not about to say players can't tell a good story without Instinctive Milestones, though I think it's clearly as good a tool as Climbing the Ladder from Requiem or the Five Questions from Don't Rest Your Head-but it must be said that on that point it's <i>all</i> on the players, where as using it takes some of the weight off, which can certainly help the vast amount of people who are intimidated by and unsure of how to even direct a Promethean game.<br /> <br /> Second, a failure to understand that you use a hammer for nails leading to an insistence on an outright demand for the change of hammer design is clearly and obviously making things harder on everyone, both involved and not involved, and actually fucks with other people who are nowhere near the original problem, which is is the order of snafu for these kind of threads(Use your context clues). Simply put, the problem that is being harped on about doesn't actually exist. Instinctive Milestones <i>work</i>. If you don't like the tool and would rather use another one, that's a totally fine and fair argument, but you cannot blame it on the tool not working. The <i>only</i> way they don't work is when you grossly misunderstand the way the tool works, and considering that the methods of entry into this branch of the hobby all go by way of a notice of the tool box setting and <i>endorsement</i> to only use any mechanic as it serves your story, there's not a failure to educate and explain on the part of the makers. Simply put, it's user error. That's not a basis for a revision, to cry and demand the establishment should work in response to the opinions presented. To do so is to further demonstrate one's lack of comprehension.<br /> <br /> Worse, all of this sets the precedence for bad storytelling to happen. Good storytellers, both players and game-mastering storytellers, tend to be good readers with strong levels of comprehension and lateral interpretation, able to apprehend information in it's correct form and application as well a broadness to comprehension that allows one to shift the apprehension to different angles and perspectives. Put more simply, readers who can understand things as they are and can also bend and flex their understanding tend to be good storytellers. They know how to creatively and correctly Tetris all the information from the group and the books into, at a minimum, an enjoyable experience, carefully fitting together things together, wisely use some pieces correctly, wisely creatively using them in wrong ways, wisely not using them when it wouldn't work, and grabbing other blocks to make the full work. Bad readers, ones with poor comprehension, likewise tend to build bad stories, using poor construction techniques with the tools they have and even ignoring the tools that could best serve them, leading to a shoddy, slammed together piece that only stays in place by the strict enforcement of the maker's hands. Rigid only by force, flimsy without hands holding it up, a storyteller with bad comprehension can only poorly create something is at, the barest minimum, three walls that cover one's head, something that only barely sets a stage for the enjoyment.<br /> <br /> These are problems that need to be addressed. Hack away all you want, but know what you're doing first. You can't break the rules if you don't even know what the rules are doing first.<br /> <br /> PS: By the way, speaking of miserable reading comprehension, it seems that, in an effort to illuminate the wisdom of &quot;There is no bad storytelling&quot; on me and others, the person trying to do this seems to have missed the note where I basically said I can't read a damn thing they're saying because I ignored them a long time ago. So, you know, I'd figured I'd be nice and blunt about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T21:44:26-07:00","id":862419,"title":"","content":"I feel that Instinctive Milestones is the kind of thing you and your Storyteller figure out together. If you have apprehensions about your Instinctive Milestones, you should have a chat with your Storyteller about it. If, after doing so, you still can't trust them, you may wish to find another Storyteller. At some point, we have to trust that our Storytellers will listen to us as players and tailor parts of the game (such as Instinctive Milestones) to us, and will be receptive to feedback about them. Otherwise, you probably shouldn't be playing with them in the first place.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Re: Bad Storytelling. I would say that bad Storytelling is one that has a harmful or anti-fun effect on anyone involved. I don't think you can pre-emptively determine what will or won't be bad Storytelling, as that varies from group to group, but I do agree it exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 04-09-2016, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T21:46:11-07:00","id":862421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862419#post862419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that Instinctive Milestones is the kind of thing you and your Storyteller figure out together. If you have apprehensions about your Instinctive Milestones, you should have a chat with your Storyteller about it. If, after doing so, you still can't trust them, you may wish to find another Storyteller. At some point, we have to trust that our Storytellers will listen to us as players and tailor parts of the game (such as Instinctive Milestones) to us, and will be receptive to feedback about them. Otherwise, you probably shouldn't be playing with them in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T22:00:56-07:00","id":862430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862148#post862148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more philosophical note I might say that there are no poor storytellers and players, only poor situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that the Storyteller that makes players frustrated because she takes no feedback from them and slowly erodes the interest in the game is a bad Storyteller, because she's letting her pride blind her from realising that players are more than a captive audience for her genius. Likewise, I'd say that a player that actively engages in antisocial behaviour despite the Storyteller's repeated pleas not to is also a bad player, because he's letting his ego eclipse his empathy.<br /> <br /> The danger with not calling out bad behaviours as bad is that they go uncorrected. The first step in correcting harmful or antisocial behaviour is identifying it. Shifting the identification of the behaviour onto the situation itself means that no individual change can happen because nobody feels like it was their responsibility. Or worse, if it's <i>everyone's</i> responsibility, you run the risk of victim-blaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T22:35:21-07:00","id":862443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861955#post861955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you don't put broccoli on pizza</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to argue with this and then I realized it was an Inside Out reference.<br /> <br /> Broccoli is a great pizza topping though. Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T22:42:57-07:00","id":862446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862405#post862405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, no, if Wyrd's response was just &quot;I don't like it, I'm not using and just gonna figure out milestones with my players,&quot; I wouldn't care. In fact, I actually assume that's gonna be the default attitude. I don't care about that.<br /> <br /> My problem is a misapprehension of the tools and their application, on two fronts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I pointed it here - on semi official topic - as I feel it design vacuum that was &quot;fixed&quot; in rest of <b>CoD </b>games by using Aspirations and in <b>Promethean</b> it will not be used ( from what we know ). I pointed at least two reasons that is valid way why something like this should be in the game and is a missed opportunity it will not. That you are not reasoning on of valid reasons from the moral high ground &quot;you should not play with people that have problems in communication with you&quot; is , in reality, your problem - cause I seen this kind situations all over the gaming community and good mechanics are for easing this things out. &quot;Talk to ST&quot; should be mantra of RPG payers - but not everyone knows it and somehow bad things and miscommunication just happens. Good mechanics make those as small as possible. With Milestones as written I see large possible Red Flags on this. I even make bold statement that this attitude was one of reasons why 1ED<b> Promethean</b> was not as successful as a game.<br /> <br /> I would not write it all on this and debate with you if it was only &quot;I will make hack of it&quot; - I feel that second valid reason - life experience decisions - is even more problematic thing in the game itself. When all your Milestones are &quot;cast from high of Principle/Demiurge&quot; it leads to misconceptions about life that you cannot do anything valuable on it by yourself. That your decisions in the end, does not matter, as all is great plan of some god in heavens ( in this take ST ) and it leads to even more separation between payers and STs at table. Created on the Pilgrimage sounds more like &quot;children in mist&quot; that cannot do anything truly with they life. And any answer on their own existence they get is more like fate with favorable factors than truly they own making.<br /> <br /> <b>If some Milestones are not chosen by <i>at least </i>player - and best would be the character - it all seems like &quot;we cannot make live of ourselves&quot;. And it is very worrisome &quot;moral&quot; of the game.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-09-2016, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T22:47:57-07:00","id":862448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862405#post862405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worse, all of this sets the precedence for bad storytelling to happen. Good storytellers, both players and game-mastering storytellers, tend to be good readers with strong levels of comprehension and lateral interpretation, able to apprehend information in it's correct form and application as well a broadness to comprehension that allows one to shift the apprehension to different angles and perspectives. Put more simply, readers who can understand things as they are and can also bend and flex their understanding tend to be good storytellers. They know how to creatively and correctly Tetris all the information from the group and the books into, at a minimum, an enjoyable experience, carefully fitting together things together, wisely use some pieces correctly, wisely creatively using them in wrong ways, wisely not using them when it wouldn't work, and grabbing other blocks to make the full work. Bad readers, ones with poor comprehension, likewise tend to build bad stories, using poor construction techniques with the tools they have and even ignoring the tools that could best serve them, leading to a shoddy, slammed together piece that only stays in place by the strict enforcement of the maker's hands. Rigid only by force, flimsy without hands holding it up, a storyteller with bad comprehension can only poorly create something is at, the barest minimum, three walls that cover one's head, something that only barely sets a stage for the enjoyment.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a more serious note, I feel I should point out that this level of complex literacy is much easier for those of us who's primary language the books are written in. While I agree with pretty much all of your assertions in this thread, I think a little leeway for folks who don't intuit English writing as naturally as we do might be in order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T22:59:25-07:00","id":862453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862446#post862446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>If some Milestones are not chosen by <i>at least </i>player - and best would be the character - it all seems like &quot;we cannot make live of ourselves&quot;. And it is very worrisome &quot;moral&quot; of the game.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans are not mortals. This is an important thing that I think you're forgetting. Prometheans are infused with Divine Fire, and this Divine Fire comes from a Divine Principle. In meta terms, that's the purview of the ST. This is much like Mummy, where there are literal divine entities telling you what to do.<br /> <br /> From a purely logical perspective, having a portion of the Milestones be in the hands of the ST, to represent the Divine Fire that all Prometheans carry inside, is perfectly reasonable. However, I think the problem is that, from an emotional perspective, this may cause a knee-jerk reaction of disempowerment and a lack of agency. I would suggest a sidebar in the book, perhaps, suggesting explicitly that these milestones can (and perhaps should) be created by the ST and the player in tandem. That ought to be a good compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:12:55-07:00","id":862461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862453#post862453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans are not mortals. This is an important thing that I think you're forgetting. Prometheans are infused with Divine Fire, and this Divine Fire comes from a Divine Principle. In meta terms, that's the purview of the ST. This is much like Mummy, where there are literal divine entities telling you what to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, Demon's got an entire subsystem of its own tied to the particulars of how you escape your connection to an angel-spawning force of unpredictable artifice as an inhuman being, and that goes a lot more specific than just what story beats you have to hit along the way from Point A to Point B.<br /> <br /> Extracting secrets from cosmic forces is neither a uniquely Promethean thing nor a thing whose precedents indicate ought to be determined in-universe, particularly for a process explicitly compared to enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:13:00-07:00","id":862462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862453#post862453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Prometheans are not mortals. This is an important thing that I think you're forgetting. Prometheans are infused with Divine Fire, and this Divine Fire comes from a Divine Principle. In meta terms, that's the purview of the ST. This is much like Mummy, where there are literal divine entities telling you what to do.<br /> <br /> From a purely logical perspective, having a portion of the Milestones be in the hands of the ST, to represent the Divine Fire that all Prometheans carry inside, is perfectly reasonable. However, I think the problem is that, from an emotional perspective, this may cause a knee-jerk reaction of disempowerment and a lack of agency. I would suggest a sidebar in the book, perhaps, suggesting explicitly that these milestones can (and perhaps should) be created by the ST and the player in tandem. That ought to be a good compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure &quot;milestones should be created by the ST and the player in tandem&quot; is the intent of the rules already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:18:03-07:00","id":862467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862461#post862461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, Demon's got an entire subsystem of its own tied to the particulars of how you escape your connection to an angel-spawning force of unpredictable artifice as an inhuman being, and that goes a lot more specific than just what story beats you have to hit along the way from Point A to Point B.<br /> <br /> Extracting secrets from cosmic forces is neither a uniquely Promethean thing nor a thing whose precedents indicate ought to be determined in-universe, particularly for a process explicitly compared to enlightenment.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact that, to my knowledge, nothing states you have to <i>want</i> or <i>enjoy</i> your Milestones. One of the Universal ones involves <i>dying</i>, so I don't think that's something most characters are going to enjoy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862462#post862462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure &quot;milestones should be created by the ST and the player in tandem&quot; is the intent of the rules already.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case, then making sure it's explicitly spelled out in the text should do the trick, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:41:12-07:00","id":862477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862448#post862448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious note, I feel I should point out that this level of complex literacy is much easier for those of us who's primary language the books are written in. While I agree with pretty much all of your assertions in this thread, I think a little leeway for folks who don't intuit English writing as naturally as we do might be in order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, and I'll even extend this to the books. It is fair to say it's not <i>always</i> the readers fault.<br /> <br /> I'm a curmudgeon, sometimes. Sorry Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:50:16-07:00","id":862479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862446#post862446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I pointed it here - on semi official topic - as I feel it design vacuum that was &quot;fixed&quot; in rest of <b>CoD </b>games by using Aspirations and in <b>Promethean</b> it will not be used ( from what we know ).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd wager that Aspirations are in Promethean 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T00:00:41-07:00","id":862484,"title":"","content":"Of that, I have no doubt. It's just that Aspirations aren't going to be sources of Vitriol. That said, I could see the Storyteller taking the character's Aspirations into account when choosing Milestones; any hint the Storyteller can get is fair game, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T00:35:46-07:00","id":862498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862484#post862484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of that, I have no doubt. It's just that Aspirations aren't going to be sources of Vitriol. That said, I could see the Storyteller taking the character's Aspirations into account when choosing Milestones; any hint the Storyteller can get is fair game, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Hack itself idea I'm thinking if Aspirations should be different from &quot;Personal Milestones&quot; ( working term for characters own Milestones )? One thing is Aspiration like &quot;Confront Centimani&quot; or &quot;Get my job back&quot;, other is &quot;Feel the love&quot; or &quot;Learn Profession&quot;. First two I would see as typical Aspirations, second to as Milestones, generating Vitriol. Still, line here is <i>very</i> fluid and I could see reasoning for marking that all fulfilled Aspirations are working Milestones and generate Vitriol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:24:57-07:00","id":862614,"title":"","content":"Completely off-topic at this point. So feel free to TL;DR.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862405#post862405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem is a misapprehension of the tools and their application, on two fronts.<br /> <br /> First, a failure to understand that you use a hammer for nails leading to an outright rejection of hammers is clearly and obviously making things harder on anyone involved, or at the least denying themselves something that will ease the process. The construction metaphor breaks a little apart, because I'm not about to say players can't tell a good story without Instinctive Milestones, though I think it's clearly as good a tool as Climbing the Ladder from Requiem or the Five Questions from Don't Rest Your Head-but it must be said that on that point it's <i>all</i> on the players, where as using it takes some of the weight off, which can certainly help the vast amount of people who are intimidated by and unsure of how to even direct a Promethean game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually this is just a bad metaphor. There are many types of hammers many of which are not intended for use on nails at all. Persistent employment of it is at best a good example of slipshod writing and at worst an indication that someone lacks a modicum of imagination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862405#post862405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, a failure to understand that you use a hammer for nails leading to an insistence on an outright demand for the change of hammer design is clearly and obviously making things harder on everyone, both involved and not involved, and actually fucks with other people who are nowhere near the original problem, which is is the order of snafu for these kind of threads(Use your context clues). Simply put, the problem that is being harped on about doesn't actually exist. Instinctive Milestones <i>work</i>. If you don't like the tool and would rather use another one, that's a totally fine and fair argument, but you cannot blame it on the tool not working. The <i>only</i> way they don't work is when you grossly misunderstand the way the tool works, and considering that the methods of entry into this branch of the hobby all go by way of a notice of the tool box setting and <i>endorsement</i> to only use any mechanic as it serves your story, there's not a failure to educate and explain on the part of the makers. Simply put, it's user error. That's not a basis for a revision, to cry and demand the establishment should work in response to the opinions presented. To do so is to further demonstrate one's lack of comprehension.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main problem is that you're making a great number of assumptions with regards to the &quot;tool.&quot; In this case the &quot;tool&quot; is comprised of some string of text. Unfortunately text is not a high-precision tool. It's not as simple as using context clues and exercising comprehension to apprehend some purpose. I think that perhaps you're assuming that writers and readers share the kind of relationship that storytellers and players do but this isn't the case at all. Writing is performative process of encoding intentions. Reading is a performative process of interpreting intentions. Unfortunately the semantics of any given string of text (or more properly the semantics of any given sentence, or paragraph if you prefer, that is referred to by a string of text) is ambiguous. The majority of human beings take this for granted, however, interpretation and thereby comprehension is a highly idiosyncratic process unique to every individual in part based on their background experiences and knowledge. To expect that all people will arrive at precisely the same understanding from some given text is to expect too much. Language is a very tricky animal. It isn't as reliable as you think it is. For example, consider the following sentence: &quot;Flying planes can be dangerous.&quot;<br /> <br /> A better metaphor for the &quot;tool(s)&quot; in this case is to liken the situation to a reference interview. The &quot;Five Questions&quot; play the role of the interviewer's questions and the shape of the Instinctive Milestones play the role of the interviewer's response to the answers given to those questions. With this metaphor it's much easier to see that the &quot;tool&quot; in question is actually two tools -- telling and listening (which in various circumstances we might reduce to a singular tool called collaboration). Successful use of these tool requires skill on both the part of the storyteller and the parts of the players. The storyteller needs to be good at listening and the players need to be good at telling.<br /> <br /> The fact is that storytellers and players are not innately &quot;good&quot; at these things. Listening and telling are skills that take time to develop and the precise nature of &quot;good&quot; falls across a rather broad continuum. A storyteller who is excellent with one group of players might be terrible with another group. The same thing is true of players. The important thing to acknowledge is that the situation isn't as simple as X is bad storytelling and Y is good storytelling. In some circumstances X may be good and Y may be bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862405#post862405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worse, all of this sets the precedence for bad storytelling to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry this isn't a court of law or a tribunal. No precedents (for bad storytelling or otherwise) are being set here. Mainly you're arguing for the sake of arguing. And at this point, so am I.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862405#post862405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good storytellers, both players and game-mastering storytellers, tend to be good readers with strong levels of comprehension and lateral interpretation, able to apprehend information in it's correct form and application as well a broadness to comprehension that allows one to shift the apprehension to different angles and perspectives. Put more simply, readers who can understand things as they are and can also bend and flex their understanding tend to be good storytellers. They know how to creatively and correctly Tetris all the information from the group and the books into, at a minimum, an enjoyable experience, carefully fitting together things together, wisely use some pieces correctly, wisely creatively using them in wrong ways, wisely not using them when it wouldn't work, and grabbing other blocks to make the full work. Bad readers, ones with poor comprehension, likewise tend to build bad stories, using poor construction techniques with the tools they have and even ignoring the tools that could best serve them, leading to a shoddy, slammed together piece that only stays in place by the strict enforcement of the maker's hands. Rigid only by force, flimsy without hands holding it up, a storyteller with bad comprehension can only poorly create something is at, the barest minimum, three walls that cover one's head, something that only barely sets a stage for the enjoyment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry it takes more than reading comprehension and knowledge of tools to tell good stories. One must also know one's audience. Frequently knowledge of audience is much more important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862405#post862405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are problems that need to be addressed. Hack away all you want, but know what you're doing first. You can't break the rules if you don't even know what the rules are doing first.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is we can (and do, as evidenced by these &quot;discussions&quot;) quibble about what the rules are doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862405#post862405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS: By the way, speaking of miserable reading comprehension, it seems that, in an effort to illuminate the wisdom of &quot;There is no bad storytelling&quot; on me and others, the person trying to do this seems to have missed the note where I basically said I can't read a damn thing they're saying because I ignored them a long time ago. So, you know, I'd figured I'd be nice and blunt about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says I'm counting on you reading this? (And obviously, you must be reading something or you wouldn't have bothered with such an oblique personal attack.) It does always amaze me how personal you make your stake in these arguments. I'm sorry if you're offended by my not taking an orthodox approach to the text but the nature of semantics permits me this leeway (plus as a storyteller I know my audience, i.e., my players, way better than you do). If people aren't interpreting what you've written the way you intended then you might consider if the problem is not with the reader but in fact with the writer. Grammar rules might be normative but I'm afraid that things like reading comprehension are idiosyncratic.<br /> <br /> Closing thoughts, you might try reading a little Frege, Grice, Russel, Chomsky, or Smith (on Chomsky) sometime. Reading comprehension doesn't actually work the way you think it does. After all, what did &quot;Flying planes can be dangerous,&quot; mean again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:18:42-07:00","id":862925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862446#post862446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>If some Milestones are not chosen by <i>at least </i>player - and best would be the character - it all seems like &quot;we cannot make live of ourselves&quot;. And it is very worrisome &quot;moral&quot; of the game.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of the game is the discovery of the Pilgrimage through the milestones, and working toward the New Dawn. How does the character picking milestones make any sense under that paradigm? <br /> <br /> Anyway, like I said over on the blog, instinctive milestones are at least directed by the player, and the player saying &quot;hey, my character should have a milestone involving ______&quot; is just good communication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:41:46-07:00","id":862986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862925#post862925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of the game is the discovery of the Pilgrimage through the milestones, and working toward the New Dawn. How does the character picking milestones make any sense under that paradigm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because discovery is not equal with trying? Like I pointed in my example before - only &quot;guessing&quot; Milestones makes Created to be puppets of outside force that want's them &quot;understand&quot; ( force ) what the meaning of their life is. That they do not makes any important decisions on they own - they can only &quot;forsake they purpose&quot; or &quot;work with purpose&quot; - it's binarity. Even <i>Destiny</i> in <b>Mage</b> or <i>Fate</i> in <b>CoD</b> rulebook is not so depressing force, letting you live contrary to them, but not marking your life unfullfiling if you are going <i>your</i> way.<br /> <br /> The idea that character strife to <i>part</i> of finding his life meaning and experience is much more correct to human life - to become adult human you need to understand power and importance of your existence decisions. Part of it is what you choose <i>has</i> meaning and that you point to your goals <i>is</i> shaping your life. If you study in collage, you work to get better job, you are spending 5 years to prepare for you life. If you change your city and move from family, to be on your own - you are making decision to shape your future relationships, to have place for other people in your life. Without that decision your life will be static and without any real meaning. You really can say &quot;God is hating me, I do not have anything to live for&quot;. And as my own example shown few posts before - it simply is untrue.<br /> <br /> If New Dawn is finding out how to be a human, grown adult, you cannot just say &quot;your life is only about finding your place in higher beings plan&quot; cause being adult is much more complex than that - and yes, part of it is that you <i>can</i> chose to make some decisions that <i>will</i> change your life. That you shape your life. Know the proverb: <i>&quot;Every man is the architekt of his own fortune&quot;</i> ? In simulation of adult life, it should at least partially true.<br /> <br /> If Milestones are secret pointers and meaningful experience on the road to Humanity, some of them chosen by character <i>need</i> to work also. Cause <i>choosing</i> them, and going with those decisions, seeing their results, it's part of experience of life!<br /> <br /> Like I pointed in my own example - my conscious decision to start looking for male lover made me now 5 years in relationship with my partner. I could just say &quot;No, I will not try, and be like rest, only lonely and bitter&quot; - and from how our society is shaped in Poland that is what whole &quot;God's plan&quot; for me to be. But I said to myself &quot;No, I will try my own thing and choose my own path&quot;.<b> In game terms I just I took and grabbed the card of previously prepared by Storyteller Milestones and shout &quot;My life will be about this!&quot;, tearing them.</b> I still look for the meaning of it, looking for the details on this path that I took - but decision I made over 6 years ago shaped me the men I'm today. It was my most important conscious venture in life - not very different how how my collage studies have shaped my work life, but <i>much</i> more important emotionally.<br /> <br /> And probably there are alternatives to what I'm now - if I did not choose to actively look for male lover, I probably be in extreme depression, or even dead, confronted with the life to this day. But I stood and said &quot;No, I will make my own fate - at least in this matter&quot;. My decision had gigantic reflect on my life as it is - and looking over this is surely my own life &quot;milestone&quot;.<br /> <br /> So how does choosing your own Milestones work with the paradigm of finding New Dawn in them? Simple - part of Milestones ( probably not much than few per character ) are based on decisions and undertakings of her. That player ( or even character ) choose alone, without Storyteller. <b>Cause at least part of our life is that what we <i>do</i> and what we <i>choos</i>e - have meaning and <i>is</i> shaping what we are as humans.</b><br /> <br /> And simplest reflecting for that - mechanically - is to make special Aspirations category ( not very different from mages Obsessions, but on other subject ) that generates Vitriol when fulfilled - and being special Milestones category.<br /> <br /> Thank you, I hoped it changed your life. ( Drops the microphone ) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ( Side note: And I mentioned many times this &quot;Milestone Aspirations&quot; should be only <i>part</i> of all characters Milestones in general - most of our life experience comes from outside force, influences and we are shaped by our environment. However, there are those few precious goals and decisions we make and those makes us who we are - and those should be working like Aspirations. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-09-2016, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T20:42:45-07:00","id":862987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862925#post862925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of the game is the discovery of the Pilgrimage through the milestones, and working toward the New Dawn. How does the character picking milestones make any sense under that paradigm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, wyrdhamster isn't asking for the <i>character</i> to choose Milestones; he's asking that the <i>player</i> be able to choose them. But yeah; that approach feels a lot like playing a detective game where the investigators are asked to choose which clues they'll find. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862925#post862925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, like I said over on the blog, instinctive milestones are at least directed by the player, and the player saying \u201chey, my character should have a milestone involving ______\u201d is just good communication.</div> </div> </div> </div>As well, I get the impression that a Milestone isn't supposed to rob the player of agency. That is, to the extent that a Milestone is a test of sorts, it's a test with multiple right answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T21:18:30-07:00","id":862996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862987#post862987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, wyrdhamster isn't asking for the <i>character</i> to choose Milestones; he's asking that the <i>player</i> be able to choose them. But yeah; that approach feels a lot like playing a detective game where the investigators are asked to choose which clues they'll find.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it is not - I'm pointing that part of Milestones should be obvious to <i>character</i> - they are his own decisions. Like in my examples - character is deciding to do something in his life, made some decision. Milestones comes from repercusion of it, from how character is evolving in her life from it. Like my looking for gay relationship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862987#post862987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, I get the impression that a Milestone isn't supposed to rob the player of agency. That is, to the extent that a Milestone is a test of sorts, it's a test with multiple right answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it <i>is</i> bit robbing when the test has wrong questions - and it cannot possible have all questions in the world, does it?<br /> <br /> I'm pointing to this - ( probable ) Five Questions will have multitde answers and made large portion of Milestones character and possible personality for Created. But in it's nature, they <b>cannot</b> answer all possible questions or topic players can raise with character in basicly Life: The Alchemy simulator. Life is too complex for that. And Pilgrimage ( from what I know ) is looking for the answers in ones life.<br /> <br /> You can easily say &quot;But ST and player can re-write them anytime they want!&quot; - on to that I answer - &quot;Yes, they can. But why they need re-write in fist place if we have such nice mechanics like Aspirations and Obsessions that easily take care of it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Making Aspiration-like Milestones ( part of all ) that players choose is much more easier and realistic than making ST and players ponder over and over again on the subjects &quot;Are we concluded everything? Will other side be satisfied with our answers? No more questions? Is there enough of Milestones?&quot; - one simpler Aspirations-like mechanics solve all those problems. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-10-2016, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:53:06-07:00","id":863035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862987#post862987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, wyrdhamster isn't asking for the <i>character</i> to choose Milestones; he's asking that the <i>player</i> be able to choose them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=861633#post861633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think it's really weird that characters, <b>in-universe</b>, cannot say &quot;I want to feel love - What will it makes me feel? Maybe it will unlock my next stage in Pilgrimage...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T23:02:49-07:00","id":863038,"title":"","content":"...wyrd, if you're so desperate, then just tell the ST to change the Milestone to whatever it is the character is trying to achieve, behind the scenes. That's in the preview. It's official.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T00:33:05-07:00","id":863060,"title":"","content":"I think it's weird that Created conscious decisions are not really Milestones. Some of them were in my life - it's seems illogical to me. And I think game miss very much without part of Milestones not being those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T01:16:30-07:00","id":863069,"title":"","content":"That's where Roles come into play, though, too. Your <i>character</i> decides on their Refinement and in doing so chooses a Role based on that Refinement. That Role is sort of their goal for the lessons they want to learn and, mechanically, the Milestones they want to achieve. So if you choose 'Guardian' as a Role then your Milestones are going to be about protecting something. <i>Your character</i> decided that. Isn't that what you want?<br /> <br /> This conversation can go deeper! We could start talking about how it's not fair that the <i>Players</i> don't reveal the storyline, settings, and NPCs because it all comes from the <i>GM</i> but where will that get us? The way you build your character and answer questions about their background, personality, skills, and opinions is going to tell the GM the kind of story you want to play. The same applies for Milestones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T09:49:17-07:00","id":863196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862986#post862986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because discovery is not equal with trying? Like I pointed in my example before - only &amp;quot;guessing&amp;quot; Milestones makes Created to be puppets of outside force that want's them &amp;quot;understand&amp;quot; ( force ) what the meaning of their life is. That they do not makes any important decisions on they own - they can only &amp;quot;forsake they purpose&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;work with purpose&amp;quot; - it's binarity. Even <i>Destiny</i> in <b>Mage</b> or <i>Fate</i> in <b>CoD</b> rulebook is not so depressing force, letting you live contrary to them, but not marking your life unfullfiling if you are going <i>your</i> way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... Prometheans <i>are</i> puppets of an outside force that wants them to understand what the meaning of their lives are. It's called The Principle. That said, it's not like they are just randomly guessing what they're supposed to do. They have Azothic Memory guiding their Pilgrimage, giving them an instinctive knowledge of how to move forward. The specifics they have to learn through trial and error, but they intuitively know what they're supposed to do in a general sense. From a meta-game perspective, the player knows what the Universal Milestones are if they've read the book, they know their Instinctive Milestones because they worked with the ST to create them, and they know the Perscribed Milestones because they're based on the character's Roles, which the player does choose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862986#post862986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that character strife to <i>part</i> of finding his life meaning and experience is much more correct to human life - to become adult human you need to understand power and importance of your existence decisions. Part of it is what you choose <i>has</i> meaning and that you point to your goals <i>is</i> shaping your life. If you study in collage, you work to get better job, you are spending 5 years to prepare for you life. If you change your city and move from family, to be on your own - you are making decision to shape your future relationships, to have place for other people in your life. Without that decision your life will be static and without any real meaning. You really can say &amp;quot;God is hating me, I do not have anything to live for&amp;quot;. And as my own example shown few posts before - it simply is untrue.<br /> <br /> If New Dawn is finding out how to be a human, grown adult, you cannot just say &amp;quot;your life is only about finding your place in higher beings plan&amp;quot; cause being adult is much more complex than that - and yes, part of it is that you <i>can</i> chose to make some decisions that <i>will</i> change your life. That you shape your life. Know the proverb: <i>&amp;quot;Every man is the architekt of his own fortune&amp;quot;</i> ? In simulation of adult life, it should at least partially true.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Promethean isn't about human children learning to be human adults, it's about beings who have no idea what it means to be human learning to be human. Being able to make those significant life decisions for one's self is the end goal of the pilgrimage, not the means by which it's carried out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862986#post862986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Milestones are secret pointers and meaningful experience on the road to Humanity, some of them chosen by character <i>need</i> to work also. Cause <i>choosing</i> them, and going with those decisions, seeing their results, it's part of experience of life!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Promethean chooses her Refinements and her Roles, and Perscribed Milestones are determined by Roles. So she <i>does</i> choose some of the lessons she wants to learn. She can't, however, choose <i>how</i> she will learn them. That's just not how learning works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862986#post862986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I pointed in my own example - my conscious decision to start looking for male lover made me now 5 years in relationship with my partner. I could just say &amp;quot;No, I will not try, and be like rest, only lonely and bitter&amp;quot; - and from how our society is shaped in Poland that is what whole &amp;quot;God's plan&amp;quot; for me to be. But I said to myself &amp;quot;No, I will try my own thing and choose my own path&amp;quot;.<b> In game terms I just I took and grabbed the card of previously prepared by Storyteller Milestones and shout &amp;quot;My life will be about this!&amp;quot;, tearing them.</b> I still look for the meaning of it, looking for the details on this path that I took - but decision I made over 6 years ago shaped me the men I'm today. It was my most important conscious venture in life - not very different how how my collage studies have shaped my work life, but <i>much</i> more important emotionally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, before I respond to this, I want to make it absolutely clear that I appreciate this is a wonderful and important moment in your life, and that is awesome. Thank you for feeling comfortable enough with this community to share such a personal revelation here.<br /> <br /> All that said, I think the way you frame this moment within the metaphor of Promethean is very telling as to your motivation for wanting player-chosen milestones. You talk about this as though God is your Storyteller and they had decided, against your wishes, that conforming with your culture's expectations of you and staying in the closet was going to be a milestone. This is <i>not</i> how it's supposed to work. The player and the storyteller are supposed to work together to create these milestones. If this metaphor was constructed in a way that matches with the way Milestones are intended to work, then coming to terms with your sexuality and deciding to seek out a partner that would make you happy would have been the Milestone that you decided on together, before the game even started, and society's expectations would have been the obstacle you had to overcome to achieve that Milestone.<br /> <br /> The way you talk about this really makes it seem like your primary motivation here is safeguarding against Storytellers who will ignore players' desires and create Milestones without their input (I won't use the term &quot;bad storytellers&quot; because that's not an argument I want to have right now, and is ultimately off-topic anyway).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862986#post862986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And probably there are alternatives to what I'm now - if I did not choose to actively look for male lover, I probably be in extreme depression, or even dead, confronted with the life to this day. But I stood and said &amp;quot;No, I will make my own fate - at least in this matter&amp;quot;. My decision had gigantic reflect on my life as it is - and looking over this is surely my own life &amp;quot;milestone&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm truly happy for you that you were able to make that choice. But you are not a Promethean and your experiences as a human learning to come into yourself as a person are really not the best baseline for a story about artificial beings that are trying to learn what it means to be human, and in doing so become human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862986#post862986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how does choosing your own Milestones work with the paradigm of finding New Dawn in them? Simple - part of Milestones ( probably not much than few per character ) are based on decisions and undertakings of her. That player ( or even character ) choose alone, without Storyteller. <b>Cause at least part of our life is that what we <i>do</i> and what we <i>choos</i>e - have meaning and <i>is</i> shaping what we are as humans.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans have some say in the path their Pilgrimages take, in the form of what Refinements they follow and what Roles they undertake within those refinements. They decide what kinds of people they want to become, but not having any experience being those kinds of people, they can't make the decision for themselves of how they will become those kinds of people. They wouldn't know where to begin. That's where Perscribed Milestones come into play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=862986#post862986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And simplest reflecting for that - mechanically - is to make special Aspirations category ( not very different from mages Obsessions, but on other subject ) that generates Vitriol when fulfilled - and being special Milestones category.<br /> <br /> Thank you, I hoped it changed your life. ( Drops the microphone ) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't think Aspirations fill the same narrative role as Milestones. Aspirations are goals, things you want to acomplish. Milestones are life lessons, experiences you need to go through before you can truly be human. You might pick &quot;hit a Milestone&quot; as an Aspiration, but you can't just decide the nature of the lesson your going to learn, or you won't really be learning anything; just reaffirming something you already knew, or at least believed to be true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T10:04:35-07:00","id":863205,"title":"","content":"asdfasdfasdf","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":2758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","user":"Errol216","date":". 04-10-2016, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:23:30-07:00","id":863704,"title":"","content":"On a different subject, I notice that Prometheans no longer (necessarily) need to create another to reach the New Dawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:35:58-07:00","id":863714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=863704#post863704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different subject, I notice that Prometheans no longer (necessarily) need to create another to reach the New Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed that as well. I am of mixed feelings on the matter. On the one hand I'm always a fan of broadening one's options, and the idea of mentoring another Promethean or creating an Athanor as a potential replacement for that milestone are pretty good alternatives. On the other hand it always seemed to fit perfectly into the Pilgrimage that one would have to create another Promethean. It simultaneously forces the Promethean to confront their own created nature, dovetails well with the milestone of confronting their own creator, and ensures that there will always be more Prometheans.<br /> <br /> That said, its still a potential milestone and I imagine that some Prometheans will procreate even without it being one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:42:57-07:00","id":863718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=863714#post863714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, its still a potential milestone and I imagine that some Prometheans will procreate even without it being one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we still don't know how the Azothic Memory works. For all we know, it could be telling the promethean that it needs to multiply and leave a part of himself behind. It's what the Milestone is about, after all. But if the Azothic Memory doesn't say more than that <i><b>and</b></i> teaches how to create other Prometheans... well, it becomes a quick and easy connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T09:49:33-07:00","id":863722,"title":"","content":"I've only had one Promethean character actually procreate. While I knew OOC that it would net me a milestone as a bonus, his IC reasoning for doing so really had nothing to do with the Pilgrimage at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T12:30:38-07:00","id":863825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=863714#post863714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, its still a potential milestone and I imagine that some Prometheans will procreate even without it being one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The procreative instinct is a big part of being human - even if not every human has it - and could be said to lie behind several of the other options presented. And the act of procreating could be important to other milestones as well, especially any deriving from Aurum or Plumbum Refinements.<br /> <br /> Writing this, it occurs to me that removing it as a necessary step for every Promethean also enables it to be used as a cooperative effort: a whole throng creates a single Promethean between them (who is presumably a new Lineage, effectively, unless they're all the same one), which has big milestone potential.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T13:48:04-07:00","id":863878,"title":"","content":"Well, it's true that in 2e, demiurges are much more of a thing. I always thought that the 1e requirement to successfully perform the generative act was more about ensuring that the Lineage would continue; but if it's now reasonably common to create a Promethean without even being one, let alone sharing its Lineage, then I don't see as much need for mandating the generative act.<br /> <br /> What I find interesting is that the implication that Extempore can't complete their Pilgrimage is very much alive and well in 2e \u2014 though the reason has changed: it's no longer because they can't replicate their generative act, but rather because they lack the Azothic Memory that provides Universal Milestones, with <i>Projectio</i> being singled out as the Universal Milestone that no Extempore has been known to complete: that is, Extempore don't come back from the dead even once.<br /> <br /> Harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T00:23:27-07:00","id":864159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=863060#post863060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's weird that Created conscious decisions are not really Milestones. Some of them were in my life - it's seems illogical to me. And I think game miss very much without part of Milestones not being those.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your decision was a Milestone in your life (or would have been, if you'd been one of the Created), and it led to something wonderful. But did you decide that that decision was going to be a Milestone in advance? I would say that a Promethean's decisions will lead them to their Milestones, rather than determine them. The Promethean chooses the road that they'll take, and that helps to determine what Milestones they'll find, but they don't decide at the beginning what they'll find along the way. A character's Aspirations should have some bearing on the Milestones, but they shouldn't determine the outcome. A Promethean with the Aspiration &quot;Become a rock star&quot; might have a Milestone of &quot;Realize that you can achieve your dreams&quot; (if the Aspiration is fulfilled) or &quot;Realize that not every dream can come true&quot; (if the Aspiration is abandoned). One that is looking for love might have Milestones related to the decision to do so, but the Milestone could be &quot;Discover that someone else can love me for who I am&quot;, &quot;Realize that some people will pretend to love you even when they don't&quot;, or &quot;Love means different things to different people&quot;. The defining moments of life come about because of our decisions, but we don't decide what is going to be a defining moment of our life in advance. We discover them as we go. We don't decide that we're going to fall in love with someone that we meet by chance during the course of our day. We go about our day, and someone new enters our life. We might not realize that meeting that person was a defining moment of our lives until years later. Milestones are the defining moments. They have to discover them, because that's the way being a human works. That's why the characters don't decide any of them in the course of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T07:35:09-07:00","id":866381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/860265-milestone-preview?p=863722#post863722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only had one Promethean character actually procreate. While I knew OOC that it would net me a milestone as a bonus, his IC reasoning for doing so really had nothing to do with the Pilgrimage at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was my experience when I ran <b>Promethean</b>, too. Once it was actually done accidentally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}